<section class="shell faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="faq-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"></p>
    <h2 id="faq-title">FAQs</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-list">
    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why cohort-based?</h3>
      <p>
        It's a fixed commitment of only a few meetings. The first cohort begins in September 2026 and runs
        until November. We plan to run more cohorts and open the community up to more people next year.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is Growth Circuit?</h3>
      <p>
        Every month, the group builds around one theme, tool, problem, or question. You explore it
        in your own time, then come together to share what you made, what broke, and what you learned.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is a Marketing Engineer?</h3>
      <p>
        A <a href="https://nicklafferty.com/blog/marketing-engineer">marketing engineer</a> is a marketer who got tired of waiting for someone else to build the
        thing they need. It is an emerging role that combines taste and curiosity with technical
        ability: writing scripts, connecting APIs, spinning up agents, and transforming manual
        processes into systems that scale.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>What about people outside New York?</h3>
      <p>
        We want Growth Circuit to reach other cities and be accessible online too. The first cohort starts
        in New York. <a href="/apply?path=global">Join the global waitlist</a> and we will reach out
        when there is something for you.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
